<title>USA: Dreyfus unveils new bond fund.</title>
<headline>Dreyfus unveils new bond fund.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dreyfus Corp said it unveiled a new fixed-income fund, the Short Term High Yield Fund, that invests in lower rated securities and maintains an effective average maturity and effective duration of three years or less.</p>
<p>Dreyfus said the fund, managed by Roger King, senior high yield portfolio manager at Dreyfus, has a 30-day yield of 11.17 percent, as of Oct 21.</p>
<p>Dreyfus is a unit of Mellon Bank Corp.</p>
</text>
